---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import DesktopDownloads from '../components/DesktopDownloads.astro';
import ProgramDirectory from '../components/ProgramDirectory.astro';
import {products} from '../data/products.mjs';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="Downloads & current releases — vibe-qc" description="Current releases of vibe-sketch, vibe-queue, vibe-qc and vibe-view. macOS and Linux standalone downloads, source installation and manuals.">
<Nav/>
<main id="main-content" class="wrap downloads">
<header class="download-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Software / current releases</span><h1>Your tools.<br/><em>Ready to work.</em></h1><p>Download all four programs with their required runtimes. Use the queue and calculation engine on the machines where your jobs run.</p><nav class="section-links" aria-label="Download sections"><a href="#published-packages">Standalone downloads ↓</a><a href="#programs">All four programs ↓</a><a href="#install-now">Source installation ↓</a><a href="#platform-notes">Platform notes ↓</a></nav></header>
<section class="download-section" aria-labelledby="published-packages"><div class="section-heading-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / Standalone downloads</span><h2 id="published-packages">Download. Open. Start working.</h2></div><p>Public website downloads.<br/>Python and application libraries included.</p></div><DesktopDownloads/></section>
<section class="download-section" aria-labelledby="programs"><span class="eyebrow">02 / The complete workflow</span><h2 id="programs">Sketch → Submit → Calculate → Analyze.</h2><p>Use each program independently or connect them. The version shown for each program identifies its current downloadable release.</p><ProgramDirectory/></section>
<section class="download-section" aria-labelledby="install-now"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Source installation</span><h2 id="install-now">For workstations, servers and development.</h2><p>Source releases on GitHub are available for vibe-qc, vibe-queue and vibe-view. Choose a release, then follow its installation guide. Every standalone download links to its matching source supplement. Each program installs separately; the four steps remain independent.</p><div class="source-grid">{['vibe-sketch','vibe-queue','vibe-qc','vibe-view'].map(id=>{const p=products.find(p=>p.id===id);return <article class="source-card"><h3>{p.name}</h3><p>{id==='vibe-queue'?'Install the command-line scheduler on your submission machine.':id==='vibe-qc'?'Install the calculation engine on the machines that run your calculations.':'Build from source when you need development features or a custom environment.'}</p><div class="route-links"><a href={p.installGuide}>Installation guide ↗</a>{p.repository?<a href={`${p.repository}/releases`}>Source releases ↗</a>:<a href="/updates/vibe-sketch/current/source.tar.gz">Matching source ↗</a>}<a href={p.licenseGuide}>{p.license} license &amp; notices ↗</a></div></article>})}</div><p>Building published source does not require a purchase or membership. The applications use MPL-2.0; bundled dependencies retain their own licenses.</p></section>
<section class="download-section" aria-labelledby="platform-notes"><span class="eyebrow">04 / Installation notes</span><h2 id="platform-notes">Choose the package for your machine.</h2><div class="notes-grid"><article><h3>macOS</h3><p>Apple Silicon (ARM64). vibe-qc requires macOS 27 or newer; the other programs require macOS 14 or newer. Open the DMG and copy the app to Applications. These builds are ad-hoc signed and not Apple-notarized; macOS may block them under its security policy.</p></article><article><h3>Linux</h3><p>Linux x86-64, tested on Debian 12. vibe-qc and vibe-queue require glibc 2.36 or newer and ship as standalone archives: extract them and run the commands in their bin directory. vibe-sketch and vibe-view use AppImages. Make the downloaded file executable and run it as a regular user. Without FUSE, use <code>--appimage-extract</code>, then launch <code>squashfs-root/AppRun</code>. Standard desktop and graphics libraries are required.</p></article><article><h3>Windows</h3><p>Paid Microsoft Store editions are planned; purchase links are not yet available. The direct downloads above are for macOS and Linux.</p></article></div><details><summary>Checksums, updates and included runtimes</summary><p>Verify SHA-256 checksums before installing. Each standalone release links to its matching source and package hashes. Download a replacement installer when a new release becomes available.</p><p>vibe-view bundles Python, PyVista, VTK, Trame and RDKit. vibe-sketch bundles Python, RDKit, QVF and the editor. vibe-queue includes Python, its CLI, daemon and web console. vibe-qc includes Python, its native engine, basis/ECP data, naming, structure fetching and D3/D4; optional ML models are separate. Bundled native libraries retain their license terms and corresponding source. These packages do not establish trusted signing, notarization or Store acceptance.</p></details><details><summary>QVF: the shared file format</summary><p>QVF remains Apache-2.0. It connects supported documents and results; it is a file format and toolkit, not a fifth desktop program. <a href="https://github.com/vibe-qc/qvf/releases">QVF source releases ↗</a></p></details></section>
</main><Footer/>
</Base>
<style>
.downloads{padding-bottom:70px}.download-heading{padding:60px 0 32px;max-width:880px}.download-heading h1{font-size:clamp(42px,6vw,76px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:20px 0}.download-heading em{color:var(--phase-pos);font-style:normal}.download-heading>p{font-size:19px;max-width:680px}.section-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 24px;margin-top:24px;font-size:14px}.download-section{padding:38px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}h2{font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.15;margin:14px 0 24px;scroll-margin-top:100px}h3{font-size:21px;margin:0 0 12px}p{color:var(--slate);line-height:1.65}a{color:var(--phase-pos);text-underline-offset:4px}.source-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px;margin:28px 0}.source-card{padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px}.route-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 20px;font-size:14px}.notes-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:28px}details{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:18px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:700px){.source-grid,.notes-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.download-heading{padding-top:35px}.section-heading-row{display:block}}
</style>
